SEG = "STO"
CAT = "fqStorage"
Q = [
    ("At home, a category A or B rifle that is not in anyone's physical possession must be stored:",
     "Unloaded, locked, bolt out", ["Unloaded, in a closed cupboard", "Loaded, in a locked safe", "Unloaded, under the bed"],
     "Section 94(2) of the Weapons Regulation 2016 requires the weapon to be stored unloaded in a locked container that meets the rules, with its bolt removed or its action broken."),
    ("A container for storing category A, B or C firearms must be a rigid structure made of:",
     "Solid steel or solid timber", ["Aluminium or a light alloy", "Chipboard or MDF sheeting", "Toughened glass or acrylic"],
     "Section 94(5)(b) requires solid steel or solid timber. The QPS storage brochure says aluminium and alloys are not compliant, and nor are chipboard, particle board, MDF or plasterboard."),
    ("A container for category D, H or R weapons must be:",
     "Solid steel, bolted down", ["Solid timber, bolted down", "Solid steel, free-standing", "Any material, if locked"],
     "Section 94(5)(a) requires a rigid structure of solid steel, bolted to the frame or floor of a permanent building. Timber is allowed only for other categories."),
    ("A category A, B or C firearm container must be fixed to the building if it weighs less than:",
     "150 kg", ["50 kg", "100 kg", "250 kg"],
     "Under s 94(5)(b)(ii), a container for these categories that weighs less than 150 kg must be securely fixed to the frame or floor of a permanent building."),
    ("A gun safe that has to be fixed in place must be secured to:",
     "A building's frame or floor", ["The wall of a garden shed", "A vehicle's chassis", "A heavy piece of furniture"],
     "Section 94(5) of the Weapons Regulation 2016 requires fixing to the frame or floor of a permanent building, so the safe cannot be carried away."),
    ("A firearm storage container must have:",
     "A sturdy keyed or combination lock", ["A magnetic childproof latch", "A cable tie through the hasp", "A sliding bolt without a lock"],
     "Section 94(6)(a) requires a sturdy combination lock, keyed lock or keyed padlock. A latch or tie is not a lock."),
    ("A firearm storage container must always be locked, except:",
     "While items go in or out", ["While someone is at home", "During daylight hours", "When the guns are unloaded"],
     "Section 94(6)(b) says the container must always be locked other than for the time needed to insert or remove a weapon, or something else, for a proper purpose."),
    ("The key to a gun safe must be:",
     "Kept from unlicensed people", ["Taped under the safe", "Left in the safe's own lock", "Hung on a hook beside the safe"],
     "Section 94(7) requires reasonable precautions so the key is not lost or stolen and is not accessible to people who are not lawfully entitled to possess the weapon."),
    ("According to the QPS storage brochure, a bolt removed for storage:",
     "Needs the gun's level of security", ["May sit on an open shelf", "Must be lodged with the police", "Must be posted to a dealer"],
     "The Queensland Police Service brochure says the bolt is the major component and is subject to the same storage requirements as the firearm, and it can be stored with the firearm."),
    ("The QPS storage brochure says ammunition must be stored:",
     "In a separate secure container", ["Loaded in the magazine", "Loose beside the firearm", "In an unlocked kitchen drawer"],
     "The QPS brochure says ammunition must be in a secure container or area separate from the container that holds the firearms. The National Firearms Safety Code also says never store firearms and ammunition together."),
    ("According to QPS, one suitable place for ammunition is:",
     "A locked inner box in the safe", ["The firearm's own magazine", "A vehicle's glove box", "An open shelf beside the safe"],
     "The QPS brochure gives a gun safe with an internal secured area for the ammunition as an example that may be suitable, because the ammunition is still locked away separately."),
    ("Which timber does QPS accept for a category A, B or C storage container?",
     "Marine ply at least 16 mm", ["Particle board of any thickness", "MDF lined with steel mesh", "Pine with ventilation holes"],
     "The QPS brochure accepts species of hardwood timber and marine ply of at least 16 mm, and rules out chipboard, particle board, MDF and plasterboard."),
    ("In the QPS storage brochure, a 'solid' container means one whose panels are:",
     "Continuous, with no holes", ["Heavy, with small air vents", "Painted inside and out", "Made of strong steel mesh"],
     "QPS says solid requires the panels to be continuous, without venting, holes or perforation."),
    ("QPS advises against installing a gun safe:",
     "In an unlocked garage", ["Inside a locked room", "Bolted to a concrete floor", "Out of sight of windows"],
     "The QPS brochure says not to install the safe where it can be readily located or seen by intruders, giving an unlocked garage or shed as the example."),
    ("QPS also advises not to leave near a gun safe:",
     "Tools that could open it", ["A list of serial numbers", "A smoke alarm", "A light switch"],
     "The QPS brochure warns against leaving power tools or other items nearby that could be used to break into the safe."),
    ("Stricter storage rules apply once one premises holds more than how many category A, B, C or D weapons?",
     "30", ["10", "20", "50"],
     "Section 94(3) of the Weapons Regulation 2016 requires the stricter part 20 storage once there are more than a total of 30 category A, B, C or D weapons, or more than 30 category H weapons."),
    ("The registered owner of a firearm must make sure secure storage is available at:",
     "The registered place", ["Any place they visit", "Their shooting club", "Their dealer's shop"],
     "Section 60(2) of the Weapons Act requires secure storage facilities to be available at the place shown in the firearms register as where the firearm is generally kept."),
    ("If your firearm is lost or stolen, you must report it to a police officer:",
     "Immediately", ["Within 14 days", "Within 28 days", "At your next renewal"],
     "Section 60A of the Weapons Act says the loss or theft must be reported to a police officer immediately the person becomes aware of it."),
    ("Under the Act, a firearm with no removable firing parts is made temporarily inoperable by:",
     "A trigger lock, key kept apart", ["Unloading it and closing it", "Putting the safety catch on", "Taking off its sling and scope"],
     "Section 8 of the Weapons Act says a firearm without a removable bolt, breech block or firing pin is made temporarily inoperable by a trigger lock whose key is securely stored separately."),
    ("Away from home, when it is unreasonable to return to your safe, a firearm not in your physical possession may be stored:",
     "Unloaded, in a locked case", ["Loaded, behind the seat", "Unloaded, on the back seat", "Unloaded, in an unlocked tent"],
     "Section 95 of the Weapons Regulation 2016 allows an unloaded weapon in a locked container, or in a closed container with the bolt removed or a trigger lock fitted, kept out of sight in a locked room, locked in a boot or locked out of sight in a vehicle."),
    ("Under s 95 of the Weapons Regulation 2016, a container holding a firearm while you are away from your safe may be:",
     "Out of sight in a locked room", ["In view in a parked car", "On a motel room balcony", "Strapped under a vehicle's tray"],
     "Section 95(3) allows the container to be out of sight in a locked room of a permanent building, locked in a vehicle's boot, or out of sight and locked in a vehicle without a boot."),
    ("A licensee in control of a weapon at a place must keep it in secure storage whenever:",
     "No one is holding or using it", ["It is dark outside", "Visitors are in the house", "It has been fired that day"],
     "Section 60(1) of the Weapons Act requires a licensee who has control of a weapon at a place to keep it in secure storage facilities when a person is not in physical possession of it."),
    ("Before putting a firearm away, the National Firearms Safety Code says to:",
     "Clean it and check it is empty", ["Leave one round chambered", "Plug the barrel with a cork", "Store its ammunition with it"],
     "The Code says to make sure the magazine and chamber are empty and clean the firearm before storage, and never to block the barrel when storing it."),
    ("When storing a pump action shotgun, the National Firearms Safety Code says not to:",
     "Remove its action", ["Empty its magazine", "Check its chamber", "Lock it away"],
     "The Code advises removing the bolt and magazine where possible, but not trying to remove the action from lever, pump action or self-loading firearms."),
]
